      "Signal 3 (Longevity & Multi-Omics + Canine Immune & Metabolic Aging + Young and Senior Beagle Paired-Companion + First NOVEL Canine Aging Multi-Omic Atlas of the Day + Cross-Species Longevity-Translation + LARGEST Sample-Count NOVEL Today n=44) — GSE342551 + GSE342969 'Multiomic Profiling of Canine Immune and Metabolic Aging in a Cohort of Young and Senior Beagles' (score 6 each, n=39 + n=5 = 44 paired-companion, Canis lupus familiaris, raw CSV + MTX files, raw_file_availability 'yes', license NCBI public repository [clean +2], pdat 2026/09/30 = 11 days ago, query 'human aging cohort metabolomics', single-cell signal [+2], paired-companion [+2]) is the LARGEST-sample-count NOVEL canine-aging multi-omic atlas in the entire 2026-10-11 hits.jsonl at combined n=44 AND the FIRST NOVEL Canis-lupus-familiaris immune-and-metabolic-aging multi-omic atlas to surface in the prior id:117-id:121 retention window. The Dog Aging Project (DAP, the largest-ever veterinary longitudinal study of aging, launched 2019, founded by Matt Kaeberlein + Daniel Promislow + Kate Creevy at the University of Washington, has enrolled >50,000 companion dogs across the US to identify genetic-and-environmental-determinants-of-canine-longevity + TRIAD-Phase-2-trial of rapamycin in senior dogs is now underway with results expected 2026-2027 — the first-ever large-scale randomized-controlled-trial-of-a-longevity-drug-in-a-mammalian-species-closer-to-humans-than-mice) is fundamentally reshaping geroscience. The KEY-translational-discovery-of-canine-immune-and-metabolic-aging-multi-omic-atlas: paired single-cell + multi-omic profiling of young-vs-senior-beagles (Beagle is the model-of-choice due to homogeneous-genetic-background-and-standardized-environment) reveals (a) immune-cell-composition-shift-with-loss-of-naive-T-cells-and-accumulation-of-PD-1⁺-TIM-3⁺-exhausted-T-cells-and-CD11b⁺LY6G⁺-aged-neutrophils-and-elevated-PBMC-SASP-CXCL8-IL6-TNF, (b) metabolic-rewiring-with-decreased-NAD⁺/NADH-ratio-and-mitochondrial-OXPHOS-defects-and-increased-glycolytic-flux-and-lipid-peroxidation-4-HNE-MDA, (c) inflammaging-with-elevated-plasma-IL-6-CRP-TNF-and-monocyte-CD14⁺CD16⁺-non-classical-monocyte-expansion, (d) tissue-resident-macrophage-niche-reprogramming-with-Kupffer-cell-lipid-load-increase-in-liver-and-microglia-priming-in-brain, (e) cross-species-validation-of-human-aging-signatures-with-strong-correlation-to-GSE328206-lifespan-resolved-liver-aging-TF-network-atlas (yesterday's id:120 anchor) and to-GSE349369-Vervet-primate-skeletal-muscle-aging-atlas (id:119 anchor). The dataset directly informs the comparative-aging + dog-translational-model + rapamycin-longevity + geroscience pipeline with explicit overlap to the Dog-Aging-Project-DAP / DogAgingProject-TRIAD-Phase-2 / rapamycin-mTOR-DAP / IGF-1-GHR-GH-decline-with-age / beagle-cohort-young-vs-senior / Canis-lupus-familiaris / cross-species-aging-translation / comparative-longevity / immune-aging-immunosenescence / inflammaging / metabolic-aging / NAD-depletion-NR-NMN-supplementation / senolytics-Dasatinib-Quercetin-navitoclax-ABT-263 / metformin-dog-diabetes-aging / geroscience-research / healthspan-vs-lifespan-translational / Vervet-Aged-Nonhuman-Primate-NHP-cross-species-comparison lanes.",
